{
  "description": "node.set (features node.set and dryRun, docs/control-port.md#nodeset-and-dry-runs): a JSON merge patch of a node's settings, made at the source, answered at the commit with what the plan applied. A dry run of each outcome (reconfigure, unchanged, restart, stored, reshape) answers it and changes nothing, tells no one and writes nothing; the real edit of the same settings is judged afresh. A key set: reconfigure (node.updated, reconfiguring with its keys, the reply, running); the same again: unchanged, and no event. null removes a key (latencyMs, which then reads its default); removing a required key is invalid-settings with the type's missing. A change of ports on a disabled node: stored, with its ports. A reshape: its dry run names the route it would remove (routes); the real edit without dropRoutes is refused ports-in-use naming every such route; with dropRoutes the route.removed, node.updated with its ports, the restart (cause reshape), and the reply with inPlace, ports and routesDropped, all in one commit.",
